        {
          "id": 687169059,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "WSUG - [Following Protocol Streams](https://www.wireshark.org/docs/wsug_html/#ChAdvFollowStreamSection)  \n```\nBack\nClose this dialog box and restore the previous display filter.\n```  \nIf I have an active display filter of `http`, do a `Follow->HTTP Stream`, see that it's not what I want and click the `Back` button, it should go back to the filtered list of packets (`http`). That might mean the text box still holds `http` but I could have foobar'ed the text box with any text before doing the `Follow`. Using that as the \"previous display filter\" doesn't seem right if I never applied it as a display filter.  \n  \nI guess the full fix would be to restore/apply the previous display filter and restore the text in edit box.  \nBut then the text box might not match the applied filter.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6701257,
            "username": "chuckcraft",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Chuck Craft",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/0809ffc6d9d98013a1895132bc055c622830b8a20bfa49328f53d5eb4a1206cb?s=80&d=identicon",
